effort` on critic_a/reconciler/judge (default unset = current behavior); new\n`tests/test_effort_thinking.py`.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 5\n\n**done-when:** Anthropic path supports `effort`, provably never sends `budget_tokens`, folds thinking\ntokens into metered output, Gemini guard untouched, suite green.\n\n- **Given** any `call_anthropic`, **then** the request contains no `budget_tokens` field. [SUBTLE â€” the 400-on-Opus-4.8 trap]\n- **Given** a response reporting thinking tokens, **then** they are folded into metered output (not dropped).\n- **Given** `effort` unset, **then** behavior + cost identical to pre-wave.\n\n## Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting to current tiers + 4.7+ tokenizer cost factor\n\n**Intent:** Retarget default model tags to current tiers (Opus 4.x / Sonnet 4.6 / Haiku 4.5) and add\nthe ~35%-more-tokens 4.7+ tokenizer factor so cost telemetry stays accurate.\n\n**Deliverables:** `kb/pricing.yaml` add the current Opus tier with cache sub-rates + `verification:`,\nreconcile `default_models`/role defaults, add `tokenizer_factor` (default 1.0; 1.35 for 4.7+); `llm.py`\napply `tokenizer_factor` ONLY to pre-call estimates, NEVER to post-call metering (real `resp.usage`\nstays ground-truth), document the distinction; `orchestrator.py` per-role defaults + role model\nconstants point to retargeted tags via existing `AURORA_*_MODEL` env overrides (no hardcode drift),\n`HAIKU_DEFAULT` stays a real priced tag; extend `tests/test_pricing_keys.py`.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 6\n\n**done-when:** All default tags resolve to priced keys, the tokenizer factor adjusts estimates only,\n`test_pricing_keys.py` passes with new tags.\n\n- **Given** every retargeted tag, **then** `lookup_rates` hits a non-$0 priced key.\n- **Given** a 4.7+ model, **then** the factor applies to estimates but NOT to recorded actuals. [SUBTLE]\n- **Given** the retargeting, **then** fallback / kill-switch / gate tests stay green.\n\n## Wave 8 â€” L6: Message Batches API for non-interactive nightly sweeps\n\n**Intent:** Opt-in async Message Batches path for the nightly sweeps (~50% discount); synchronous path\nstays the default; correct batch-discounted metering preserved.\n\n**Deliverables:** `llm.py` `submit_anthropic_batch(...)` + poll/collect reusing `_is_retryable_anthropic`,\neach result recording `CostRecorder.record(... batch_mode=True)` from real per-result usage (incl. Wave-4\ncache fields); a single-request batch failure degrades to synchronous `call_anthropic` (`batch_mode=False`)\nvia `_note_degrade` (the sweep never aborts); `orchestrator.py` `walk_pipeline` behind\n`AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` (default off) collecting the per-candidate critic_a/reconciler/judge Anthropic\ncalls into one batch/sweep (flag-off path byte-for-byte the current synchronous pipeline; a missing\nsecurity-judge batch result maps to `abstain`, fail-closed); Gemini path + kill-switch unchanged; new\n`tests/test_batch_sweep.py`.\n\n**Depends on:** Wave 7\n\n**done-when:** The opt-in batch path meters each result at the 50%-discounted rate, degrades per-item on\nfailure, keeps the gate fail-closed, and leaves the default (flag-off) pipeline + all tests unchanged.\n\n- **Given** a collected batch result, **then** its `costs` row has `batch_mode=1` and `usd_estimate` exactly 0.5Ã— the synchronous equivalent. [SUBTLE]\n- **Given** one batched request fails, **then** it falls back to synchronous (metered `batch_mode=0`), the degrade counter increments, the run can close `partial`.\n- **Given** `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP` unset, **then** pipeline + recorded costs identical to pre-wave; a missing security-judge result fails closed to `abstain`.\n","numLines":221,"startLine":1,"totalLines":221}}}
