{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01WCt4FZ3ZVUazRbmafoagL1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## foreman-handoff-phase2 â€” Grounded bullet claims\n\n**North Star & scope guardrails**\n- The plan closes two security/judgment tripwires on Aurora's LIVE verdict path *and* adopts cheap modern Anthropic capabilities â€” explicitly **evolving `llm.py` + the security path, not rebuilding the architecture**.\n- Locked-preserved (untouched): KB schema + library, single-owner security gate (`roles/security/gate.py`), deterministic cost telemetry (CostRecorderâ†’`pricing.yaml`), Helping Hand, and the publisher.\n- Hard invariant across both security waves: **no seam may produce an unearned pass** on the live verdict path.\n- Two live-impacting steps are **separately authorized and OUT of these waves**: the metered evidence-shadow batch (SA-1) and the live promotion flip (SA-2).\n- **No test weakening** anywhere â€” the test count may only rise.\n\n**Structure**\n- 8 waves run **in series** (they overlap on `orchestrator.py` + the security judge). Waves 1â€“2 = security hardening; Waves 3â€“8 = `llm.py` upgrades, with the cost-telemetry substrate landing first so discount features are metered correctly.\n- Source plans: `docs/AURORA_HARDENING_PLAN.md` and `docs/AURORA_LLM_UPGRADES_PLAN.md`. Test command: `python -m pytest`.\n\n**Wave 1 â€” H1: Payload-depth security scan**\n- Replaces the W2 served-text baseline (artifacts stamped `clean-with-notes` from name + short_description) with a scan of each artifact's **real payload, re-fetched from `canonical_url`**, re-stamping `security_status` so enforce mode reflects payload truth.\n- Verified constraint: payloads are **not retained on disk** (`payload_files` lazy + empty), so the scan must re-fetch â€” reusing existing machinery in `bin/run_security_shadow.py::_run_pipeline` (7-day tarball cache).\n- Deterministic-only, **no LLM cost** (judge/sandbox default-off). Re-stamp is **monotonic toward non-servable** (worst-wins via `gate._worst_status`); clean rows untouched.\n- Failed/stale fetch â†’ `extraction-incomplete`, fail-closed to quarantine (where not a relaxation), surfaced in audit.\n- Scannable set â‰ˆ **775 artifacts** (`retired_at IS NULL AND kind IN ('skill','tool','agent','model')`). New CLI `bin/scan_payload_depth.py` with `--limit/--dry-run/--audit-out`. Depends on: none.\n\n**Wave 2 â€” H2: Evidence-loop promotion machinery**\n- Makes the W3 evidence loop promotable: a **real per-iteration LLM `score_fn`** (replacing `make_precomputed_score_fn`) re-running the critic panel over the payload-deepened corpus, every call metered through `cost_recorder` (no CostRecorder bypass).\n- Adds runnable `bin/engine-diff.py` emitting GO/NO-GO that enforces **all four thresholds**: agreement â‰¥ 0.95, min_samples â‰¥ 200, unearned == 0, cost â‰¤ 1.5Ã—.\n- Metered shadow-batch command built + unit-tested here, but the **live run is SA-1 (out of scope)**.\n- Promotion switch wired but **defaults to legacy** (`AURORA_EVIDENCE_ENGINE=legacy|loop`), honoring the 1-week rollback. **The flip is NOT performed here (SA-2).** Loop structurally cannot emit an unearned pass; non-convergence force-downgrades `pass`â†’`flag`. Depends on: Wave 1.\n\n**Wave 3 â€” L1: Cost-telemetry substrate (safety-first)**\n- Migration `0024_costs_cache_batch.sql` adds nullable `cache_read_tokens`, `cache_write_tokens`, `batch_mode` columns (mirrored in `schema.sql`); `pricing.yaml` gains cache sub-rates (cache-read â‰ˆ0.1Ã— input, cache-write â‰ˆ1.25Ã— input) and `batch_discount: 0.5`.\n- `CostRecorder.record` gains optional cache/batch args; **legacy 4-arg call sites must be byte-for-byte identical**. Lands *before* any feature emits cache/batch tokens. Depends on: Wave 2.\n\n**Wave 4 â€” L2: Prompt caching on repeated critic/judge prefixes**\n- Applies `cache_control:{\"type\":\"ephemeral\"}` to stable system+rubric prefixes (critic_a, security judge, reconciler); Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback carries the same cache_control; cache tokens metered at Wave-3 rates. Caching disabled â‡’ cost equals pre-wave. Depends on: Wave 3.\n\n**Wave 5 â€” L3: Structured outputs for critic/security/KB-extraction JSON**\n- Replaces brittle `json.loads(strip_fences(...))` with schema-guaranteed JSON on critic/reconciler/security-judge paths; one shared verdict schema in `roles/contracts.py`. Gemini paths (critic_b Gemini branch, `langextract_adapter.py`) stay as-is. Off-schema judge response still **fails closed to `abstain`**. Depends on: Wave 4.\n\n**Wave 6 â€” L4: Adaptive thinking via `effort`**\n- Adopts `effort`-based adaptive thinking; **never sends `budget_tokens`** (deprecated on 4.6+; Opus 4.8 returns 400) â€” enforced by a guard that fails loudly. Folds API-reported thinking tokens into metered output (root cause of the prior **$118 incident**). `effort` unset â‡’ behavior + cost identical to pre-wave. Depends on: Wave 5.\n\n**Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting + 4.7+ tokenizer factor**\n- Retargets default tags to current tiers (Opus 4.x / Sonnet 4.6 / Haiku 4.5) and adds `tokenizer_factor` (default 1.0; **1.35 for 4.7+**) applied **only to pre-call estimates, never to post-call metering** (real `resp.usage` stays ground-truth). All default tags must resolve to priced keys. Depends on: Wave 6.\n\n**Wave 8 â€” L6: Message Batches API for nightly sweeps**\n- Adds opt-in async batch path (`submit_anthropic_batch` + poll/collect) behind `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` (**default off**), metering each result at the **0.5Ã— batch-discounted rate**. Per-item failure degrades to synchronous `call_anthropic` (run never aborts); a missing security-judge batch result maps to `abstain` (fail-closed). Flag-off path is byte-for-byte the current synchronous pipeline. Depends on: Wave 7.\n\nWant me to also save this as an Aurora memory artifact, or is the summary alone enough?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"i